            {
                "drawing_id": "257f1cc6-4d54-4362-8c03-d87667680521",
                "locked": false,
                "rotation": 0,
                "svg": "<svg width=\"520\" height=\"827\"><text font-family=\"TypeWriter\" font-size=\"10.0\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#00ff00\" fill-opacity=\"1.0\">vlan database \nvlan 10\nvlan 20\nvlan 30\nvlan 40\nvlan50\nexit\nconfigure terminal\nip routing(em tds os ESW)\ninterface f1/0\nswitchport mode access \nswitchport mode access  vlan10\ninterface f1/1\nswitchport mode access \nswitchport mode access  vlan20\ninterface f1/15\nswitchport mode trunk \nswitchport trunk allowed vlan 1,10,20,50,1002-1005\n\n\ninterface vlan10\nno shutdown\nno autostate(em alguns computadores configuramos a vlan\n e ela fica down, este comando serve para que\nmesmo que a vlan nao tenha atividade ela fica sempre up)\nip address 192.10.1.10 255.255.255.0\ninterface vlan20\nno shutdown\nno autostate\nip address 192.20.1.10 255.255.255.0\ninterface vlan50\nno shutdown\nno autostate\nip address 192.1.1.10 255.255.255.0\n\nend\nwrite\n ESW2\n</text></svg>",
                "x": 142,
                "y": -858,
                "z": 2
            },
